# Medora enterprise patient & facility identity invariant

Permanent architectural contract for **all** current and future service lines.

```
ONE FACILITY
  → ONE REGISTRATION ENGINE
  → ONE PATIENT / MRN AUTHORITY
  → ONE MEDICAL RECORD
  → MANY SERVICE LINES
```

A **service line** is a capability/workspace under the existing facility. It is **never** a separate patient identity or registration universe.

Service lines include (non-exhaustive): Clinic, Dental, Emergency, Hospital, Observation, Inpatient, Laboratory, Radiology, Pharmacy, Urgent Care, Behavioral Health, Pediatrics, future specialties.

## MUST

1. **Same `facilityId`** when enabling new service lines — never clone the organization.
2. **Same enterprise Registration** for every service line; a registered patient is discoverable by any authorized line in that facility.
3. **Same `Patient` authority** — no `DentalPatient` / `ClinicPatient` / `HospitalPatient` / `EmergencyPatient`.
4. **Same MRN** — no second MRN because the patient later receives Dental, Clinic, ED, Hospital, etc.
5. **Enterprise patient search** in every authorized service-line workspace — do **not** limit search to patients who already have an encounter in that line (e.g. Clinic-registered, never-seen-in-Dental → still searchable from Dental).
6. **Patient.id only for mutations** — free-text search/name/MRN fragments must **never** be substituted as `Patient.id` in URLs or encounter create paths. Selection of a search hit establishes `selectedPatient.id`; encounter POST uses that UUID only.
7. **Enterprise Encounter** + service-line context (e.g. Dental tag) — never `DentalEncounter` as a parallel identity.
8. **One longitudinal Patient Medical Record** holding Clinic / Dental / ED / Hospital encounters under the same patient.
9. **Historical integrity** — enable/disable service lines must not rewrite patient identity, MRN, encounters, documents, orders, results, billing, odontogram findings, closed charts, or audit history.
10. **Department rows** (e.g. `DepartmentCode.DENTAL`) are operational routing under the same facility — not a new patient/facility authority.
11. **Specialties** (e.g. Orthodontics under DENTAL) are configuration under the service line — not separate facilities or patients.
12. **Billing** may use service-line context for classification/reporting — never a separate patient identity.
13. **Audit** attributes activity to same `facilityId`, `patientId`, `encounterId`, service-line context, actor, timestamp.

## STOP — architectural review required

Do **not** implement without review:

`DentalPatient` · `DentalRegistration` · `DentalMRN` · `DentalFacility` · `ClinicPatient` · `HospitalPatient` · `EmergencyPatient` · service-line-specific patient table · service-line-specific registration engine · `ClinicFacility` / `HospitalFacility` clones for a new service

## Dental-specific

Dental discovery uses the **enterprise Patient** authority (after normal search threshold + facility auth). A prior Dental encounter is **not** required to appear in Dental search.

## Certification (every new service-line milestone)

Prove: same `facilityId` · same `patientId` · same MRN · shared Registration · shared Patient search · shared Medical Record · enterprise Encounter reuse · no patient duplication · no facility cloning.

**Contract:** ONE PATIENT · ONE REGISTRATION · ONE MRN · ONE MEDICAL RECORD · ONE FACILITY · MANY SERVICE LINES.
